<!--
  Lint runs in CI (.github/workflows/check.yml) and aborts the build on errors. This file
  silences the two errors the 2019 code reports, each for a stated reason and as narrowly as
  lint allows. Everything else lint finds - 52 warnings and one informational note, listed in
  UPGRADE-NOTES.md section 4 - stays visible in the uploaded report; warnings do not fail the
  build, so they never needed silencing.

  There is no lint baseline file on purpose: a baseline would freeze all 55 findings, including
  the 52 that could never fail anything, and hide any new warning among them.
  -->
<lint>

    <!--
      Raised by com.bumptech.glide.request.target.NotificationTarget, a Glide class this app
      never references: nothing here posts a notification (grep for NotificationTarget or
      NotificationManager returns nothing outside the library). The "fix" lint suggests is to
      declare POST_NOTIFICATIONS, which would ask users for a permission the app does not use
      and would show up on the Play listing. The dependency disappears in the 2.0 rewrite
      (Glide gives way to Coil), and with it this finding.

      This one cannot be scoped to a path: lint reports it against the merged manifest as a
      whole, with no element or line to attach tools:ignore to.
      -->
    <issue id="NotificationPermission" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      A real bug, and a deliberately unfixed one: SettingsFragment builds the feedback email
      subject across two lines without a "+", so the second line is computed and thrown away
      and the subject loses the app subtitle. It is recorded as known behaviour K9 in
      docs/BEHAVIOUR.md and in UPGRADE-NOTES.md section 8, and the rewrite decides it in the
      pull request that touches that screen - this stage does not change behaviour in the 2019
      code. Adding the "+" would change what a user's email client shows.

      Scoped to that one file, so the same mistake anywhere else still fails the build.
      -->
    <issue id="SuspiciousIndentation">
        <ignore path="src/main/java/com/baruckis/kriptofolio/ui/settings/SettingsFragment.kt" />
    </issue>

</lint>
